    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482-a1">

                <pb facs="0499" n="1233" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1233"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 526.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mrs. Dodd to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American College for Girls</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>[, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            type="content-date" when="1895-04-05"
                    >undated</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p>At a meeting of the faculty of the American College for Girls in Constantinople,
                    held on the 5th of April, 1895, the following resolution was passed: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Whereas, the American College for Girls has received from His Imperial
                            Majesty the Sultan of Turkey an irade, by which all taxes are forever
                            remitted upon the property of the college,</p>
                        <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That the faculty express their
                            sincere gratitude to the Hon. A. W. Terrell, minister plenipotentiary of
                            the United States, for his untiring and successful efforts to obtain
                            this irade.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Isabel F. Dodd</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Faculty.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
